cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and report the analysis settings (download the summary from the Data Summary tab)."
title: "Qualitative Text Analyzer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adegoke
    given-names: Hope
  - family-names: Anyaibe
    given-names: Oluchi
version: 2.0.0
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hope112/Qual_Text_Analyzer"
url: "https://diodnl-hope-adegoke.shinyapps.io/Qualitative_Analysis/"
abstract: >-
  An R Shiny app for exploring open-ended text such as survey responses:
  word frequencies, lexicon-based sentiment (Bing), and latent Dirichlet
  allocation topic modeling with relevance-ranked terms, document-topic
  shares, and diagnostics for choosing the number of topics.
keywords:
  - qualitative data analysis
  - text mining
  - topic modeling
  - latent Dirichlet allocation
  - sentiment analysis
  - R Shiny
